# Tasks: Scribble Single-Round Game Completion

**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-scribble-single-round-game/`

**Prerequisites**: plan.md (required), spec.md (required for user stories)

**Tests**: Manual browser-based validation is required by the feature specification. Add automated tests only if the existing repository already supports them with low effort.

**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story to enable independent implementation and testing of each story.

## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`

- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies)
- **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (e.g., US1, US2, US3, US4)
- Include exact file paths in descriptions where the repository paths are known; replace placeholders with actual starter paths after inspection.

## Path Conventions

- **Web app**: `backend/src/`, `frontend/src/`
- Use actual starter file paths after discovery if they differ from the plan assumptions.

## Phase 1: Setup (Shared Infrastructure)

**Purpose**: Repository inspection and documentation alignment

- [ ] T001 Inspect actual backend files for room model, room store, and room API handlers under `backend/src/`.
- [ ] T002 Inspect actual frontend files for create room, join room, lobby, game placeholder, and API helpers under `frontend/src/`.
- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm local run flow for backend and frontend and verify starter happy path manually.
- [ ] T004 Update `/specs/001-scribble-single-round-game/spec.md`, `plan.md`, and `tasks.md` with exact starter file paths if they differ from assumptions.

***

## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)

**Purpose**: Core shared infrastructure required before any scenario-specific work

**⚠️ CRITICAL**: No user story work can begin until this phase is complete

- [ ] T005 Create or extend shared room/player/round types in `backend/src/...` and `frontend/src/types/...`.
- [ ] T006 [P] Add shared backend validation helpers for trimmed names, normalized room codes, and normalized guesses in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T007 [P] Add or update frontend API/service helpers for passing `roomCode` and lightweight `playerId` in `frontend/src/services/...` or equivalent.
- [ ] T008 Create or extend a frontend identity persistence helper for `roomCode`, `playerId`, and `playerName` in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T009 Establish shared round phase values (`lobby`, `playing`, `result`) in backend and frontend contracts.

**Checkpoint**: Foundation ready — user story work can now begin in sequence or parallel where safe

***

## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Room setup and lobby readiness (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Deliver reliable room creation/joining, host tracking, lobby polling, and host-only start gating.

**Independent Test**: Create a room in tab A, join it from tab B, verify auto-updating lobby membership, validate blank-name and invalid-room-code errors, and verify host-only start with a 2-player minimum.

### Implementation for User Story 1

- [ ] T010 [P] [US1] Extend player state with `id`, `isHost`, and `score` in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T011 [US1] Update create-room handler in `backend/src/...` to trim name, reject empty input, create host player, and return player identity.
- [ ] T012 [US1] Update join-room handler in `backend/src/...` to trim name, normalize room code, reject invalid code, and return player identity.
- [ ] T013 [US1] Update room fetch handler in `backend/src/...` to return current room snapshot for polling.
- [ ] T014 [US1] Add start-game endpoint skeleton in `backend/src/...` with host-only check and minimum-two-player validation.
- [ ] T015 [P] [US1] Update create-room UI in `frontend/src/...` to trim input and show validation errors.
- [ ] T016 [P] [US1] Update join-room UI in `frontend/src/...` to trim input and show validation errors.
- [ ] T017 [US1] Persist `roomCode`, `playerId`, and `playerName` after successful create/join in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T018 [US1] Add lobby polling every ~2 seconds with cleanup in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T019 [US1] Render host badge or label in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T020 [US1] Render start action for host only and show clear feedback when start is not allowed in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T021 [US1] Validate room isolation manually with a second room code.

**Checkpoint**: User Story 1 is fully functional and independently testable

***

## Phase 4: User Story 2 - Game start and drawer visibility (Priority: P2)

**Goal**: Start a round with deterministic drawer assignment, deterministic secret word selection, drawer-only word visibility, and zeroed scores.

**Independent Test**: Start a room with at least two players, verify that host becomes drawer, confirm only the drawer sees the word, and confirm all scores start at 0.

### Implementation for User Story 2

- [ ] T022 [US2] Add `RoundState` to room model in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T023 [US2] Implement deterministic drawer assignment in start-game handler in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T024 [US2] Implement deterministic word selection from starter list in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T025 [US2] Update start-game handler to set phase to `playing` and zero scores in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T026 [US2] Update room fetch handler in `backend/src/...` to shape response by `playerId` and hide secret word from guessers.
- [ ] T027 [US2] Update lobby/game transition logic in `frontend/src/...` to react to `phase` changes.
- [ ] T028 [US2] Render drawer identity clearly in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T029 [US2] Render secret word only for drawer in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T030 [US2] Render zeroed scoreboard on game start in `frontend/src/...`.

**Checkpoint**: User Stories 1 and 2 work independently and together

***

## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Drawing, guessing, and scoring (Priority: P3)

**Goal**: Replace placeholders with playable round interaction including drawing, guess submission, synchronized history, and score updates.

**Independent Test**: Have the drawer draw and clear the canvas, have a guesser submit blank, wrong, and correct guesses, and confirm history and scoring behavior on both tabs.

### Implementation for User Story 3

- [ ] T031 [US3] Add drawing update endpoint in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T032 [US3] Add drawing clear endpoint in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T033 [US3] Restrict drawing mutations to the drawer in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T034 [US3] Add guess submission endpoint in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T035 [US3] Normalize guesses with `trim().toLowerCase()` and reject empty guesses in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T036 [US3] Append guesses to shared history in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T037 [US3] Award 100 points for first correct guess and 0 for incorrect guesses in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T038 [US3] End round on first correct guess and store winner in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T039 [US3] Replace placeholder canvas with drawing component in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T040 [US3] Wire drawer drawing updates and clear action in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T041 [US3] Render read-only shared drawing for non-drawers in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T042 [US3] Implement guess form with validation in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T043 [US3] Render guess history for all players in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T044 [US3] Render live scoreboard in `frontend/src/...`.

**Checkpoint**: User Stories 1, 2, and 3 work independently and as a full playable round

***

## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Result state and restart (Priority: P4)

**Goal**: Complete the single-round lifecycle with result presentation and host-controlled restart back to lobby.

**Independent Test**: Finish a round via a correct guess, verify result content in both tabs, restart from host tab, and confirm players remain while round-specific state is cleared.

### Implementation for User Story 4

- [ ] T045 [US4] Ensure result-phase room snapshot includes correct word, final scores, guess history, and winner in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T046 [US4] Add restart endpoint in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T047 [US4] Restrict restart to host in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T048 [US4] Preserve players and host identity while clearing round-specific state in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T049 [US4] Return room phase to `lobby` on restart in `backend/src/...`.
- [ ] T050 [US4] Render result UI with correct word, final scores, and guess history in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T051 [US4] Render restart action for host only in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T052 [US4] Return all players to lobby after restart in `frontend/src/...`.
- [ ] T053 [US4] Verify old drawing, old guesses, and old winner state are cleared after restart in `frontend/src/...`.

**Checkpoint**: All four user stories are independently functional and the full round lifecycle is complete

